title Caravan precede -- a turn may name a turn, and the plan closes them once
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Microkernel Target double-seat, Standfast on reds first, send each finished increment as its own signed round
think Standfast first. crux/REDS.md holds 83 rows and every open note reads closed and released -- 81, 83, 84, 85, 87 each with a witness standing behind the claim. Ran the two guards that watch this class rather than trusting the notes: witness_claim_check_witness GREEN over all runnable tools/*.rish, and the living-card ASCII check clean over the new prose. No agent-closable red stood, so the line was clear for constructive work.
think The running thread came from the three newest logs rather than from REMEMBER alone. phases.rye recommended asking whether a phase may name the phases it depends on; fence.rye answered with a prefix and recommended asking what a prefix cannot express; mask.rye answered with a set in one word and recommended the honest next crux plainly -- every reading in the arc orders phases inside one turn and reads strangers by their regions alone, so a turn that must follow another turn has no word for it. That is this lap.
think The shape came from the elder rung rather than from a new idea. A turn is the same small thing a phase's siblings were: max_queue_len is sixteen, so a queue can never cut its work into more than sixteen turns, and the set of turns a turn follows fits the same u32 a sibling mask fits. So the whole move is one tier up at the same price -- one forward pass at the door, one bit test after.
think The cycle question is where a tier-up could have grown the graph. A sibling mask was safe because a turn's steps are written in order, so a single forward pass suffices. Turns carry no such guarantee from the plan's writing order, so the rule became direction itself: a turn may name only turns numbered below it, read once at the door by turns_are_sound. That rules out every cycle by construction, and the closing walks turn numbers upward once with no visited set, no stack, and no second pass.
think A second door check was needed that the elder rungs never wanted. A cross-turn order is a fact about turns rather than about phases, so turns_speak_once refuses a plan whose phases of one turn disagree about what that turn follows -- otherwise one question would carry two answers and the reading would depend on which phase was asked.
think The lap had to span domains and turns at once. Every elder rung's lap could not have measured this: two turns with no shared region and different domains are free under every reading before this one. So client_a opens with a place and three more turns of its own domain queue behind it, which blocks the head and makes a pass the only way forward; turn 4 has client_b place into ask_b and names turn 3; turn 5 has client_c peek the published menu and names turn 4 alone, following turn 3 only through the closing; turn 6 has client_b peek back_b and names nothing, which leaves exactly one lawful pass standing under the preceded reading.
obs The cost is named rather than hidden, because there is no gain to report. A cross-turn order is a constraint, so it can only take passes away -- 3 passes by act and masked against 1 preceded, and 4 slots unspent against 6. What this rung buys is an order that was previously unwritable and a supervisor that keeps it; the slot is spent knowingly, safety first in TAME order. A rung reporting only a gain would have been dishonest here.
obs The numbers say it in one line: the preceded lap breaks a named turn 2 times by act, 2 masked, 0 preceded. The elder reading cannot see the order at all, which is exactly why the word was needed, and the preceded reading keeps it without exception under its own invariant on metal.
obs An empty turn mask is the sibling mask exactly, proven pair by pair over the whole lap, so this rung generalizes mask.rye rather than rivalling it -- the same relationship a full sibling mask had to the fence and the link. The closing proof mirrors its elder too: turn 5 names turn 4 alone and binds turn 3 only after closing, and a turn nobody named stays unbound.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. Dropping the turn order from items_contend reds the pure read at a phase inside a named turn being free to pass it, caught in the happy zone before a single child starts. Keeping the order and hiding it from the choosing alone fires the preceded run's own fill_table invariant at caravan/precede.rye:616, so that assert is load-bearing rather than decorative.
obs The isolation half needed nothing again, and for a new reason this time. The elder rungs were quiet there because two phases of one turn share a domain and commute.admissible refuses to stand a domain beside itself. Here two phases of two turns may genuinely stand at one instant, and commute already answers that whole question from the regions the document declares -- so a cross-turn order tightens the order room alone.
obs Council rota lap 473 mod 27 = 14 -- Radiant Style with Twilight, read deep. Its playbook shaped the prose directly: the module banner leads with what the rung is rather than what its elder lacked, the cost paragraph states the price affirmatively rather than as a disclaimer, and the technical README section ends plainly, spending no benediction it had not earned.
obs Thirty-four green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- style bans clean, width-check exit 0 -- and the neighbor rung re-GREEN: caravan_mask_witness passed unchanged beside the new one.
loom witness=caravan_precede_witness children=7 turns=7 passes_by_act=3 passes_masked=3 passes_preceded=1 slots_unspent_by_act=4 slots_unspent_masked=4 slots_unspent_preceded=6 out_of_precede_by_act=2 out_of_precede_masked=2 out_of_precede_preceded=0
file caravan/precede.rye a turn names the turns it follows in one word, the plan closes them once at the door, direction rules out every cycle without a walk
file tools/caravan_precede_witness.rish proves the finding and its price on metal, reading every claim natively per the REDS #85 loom
file caravan/README.md the rung's durable record, so the doc and the behavior move in one commit
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is what a turn mask still cannot say about the shape of the plan itself -- every reading in this arc takes the queue's written order as given and only ever loosens or tightens which pairs may be swapped, so a plan whose turns are written in an order no author intended is kept faithfully in the wrong order, and the question becomes whether the queue may derive its own head order from the names already written rather than trusting the sequence it was handed, which wants a lap measuring what a derived order costs against the one the author typed
